Build synthetic layers that publish token vectors: an embedding and an argmax.

Part of the SASH eb95bfa build that verifiable-inference-ethereum proves its
synthetic bundle corpus with (SPEC.md §1.1). Prover only: both changes sit in
the CLI and in layer.rs's `prover`-gated `impl Layer`, so the verifier build the
segment guest runs is unchanged. Upstream source is Apache-2.0; this patch
modifies it (Apache-2.0 §4(b)).

No upstream synthetic layer has an embedding table or an argmax key column:
the synthetic head proves with --unsound-skip-argmax, and a layer-0 synthetic
chunk with --unsound-skip-embedding. So no synthetic bundle publishes a token
vector, and patch 0006's token binding, which only a chunk with a token vector
exercises, cannot be tested on the corpus.

- prover/src/layer.rs: `Layer::synth_embed(vocab)` gives a synthetic layer
  with the wiring family a `(vocab, d)` embedding table and `tok_in`: position
  `t` reads id `(3 + 7 t) mod vocab` (distinct ids are asserted), whose row is
  the family's own input row `t`; every other row is zero.
  `Layer::synth_argmax(round)` gives a synthetic head chunk `head_keys`, the
  order key of the `lm_head` dequant's output under the plan's spec (`deq_ref`
  reads only `variant` and `round`, as `synth_family` already relies on), and
  `head_tok`, each row's first maximum: what a dump's `key_head.u16` and
  `tok_head.i32` hold.
- prover/src/cli.rs: the switches `--synth-embed` (with `--synth-embed-vocab`,
  default 64) and `--synth-argmax`, after `--synth-head`, like it
  witness-construction switches: without them a synthetic layer composes
  exactly as it always did, and every digest upstream pins is unchanged.

